# Repo-root .dockerignore — for `docker build -f worker/Dockerfile .` (the ingestion
# worker image; see worker/Dockerfile for why its build context is the repo root and not
# worker/). Vercel builds the Next app and does not use Docker, so this file affects the
# worker image only.
#
# Keep this an EXCLUDE list, never an allowlist: an allowlist that forgets a directory
# turns into a missing-file build error, but a stale exclude here would silently ship
# stale code. Everything the image actually needs is enumerated by the Dockerfile's COPY
# lines; this file only stops the context from carrying things nothing copies.

# Dependency trees — reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output (host artefacts must never leak into the image).
.next
dist
worker/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
out
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# VCS / tooling / editor state.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Local environment + anything secret-shaped. The worker gets its configuration from Fly
# secrets at runtime, never from a file baked into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not used by the worker runtime.
.scratch
docs
evals
tests
supabase/local-dev
playwright.config.ts
